  "fragment": "<div class=\"bridge\"><span>And somewhere in Arizona,</span><p>the mail has legs.</p></div>\n<section class=\"mail-story\" id=\"mail\" aria-labelledby=\"mail-title\">\n<div class=\"mail-intro\"><div class=\"mail-copy\"><h2 id=\"mail-title\">The last<br><span class=\"nine\">9</span><span class=\"miles\">miles.</span></h2><p>For Supai, home of the Havasupai people, the mail’s final leg is a mule train.</p></div><div class=\"mule-scene\"><div class=\"postmark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">SUPAI, AZ<span>U.S. MAIL</span></div><img src=\"assets/mule.webp\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"Illustrated mule carrying mail panniers\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"mule-caption\">Special delivery. Four-legged edition.</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"journey-story\"><div class=\"journey-intro\"><h3>Getting there is<br>only half the trip.</h3><p>Three hours down the canyon.<br>Five hours to climb back out.</p><button class=\"round-link\" id=\"replay-journey\">Watch the round trip <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span></button></div><div class=\"journey-score\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three hours to descend to Supai, then five hours to return. Eight equal marks each represent one hour.\"><div class=\"journey-leg down\"><div><span>To Supai</span><strong>3<span>h</span></strong></div><div class=\"hour-marks\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div><div class=\"journey-leg up\"><div><span>Back to the rim</span><strong>5<span>h</span></strong></div><div class=\"hour-marks\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div><p id=\"journey-status\" aria-live=\"polite\">A longer journey home.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"mail-bottom\"><p><strong>10–22 mules.</strong> Five days a week.</p><details class=\"source\"><summary>The receipts</summary><p><a href=\"https://facts.usps.com/fun/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">USPS Postal Facts, May 2026 ↗</a><br>USPS reports the nine-mile route, mule count, delivery days, and three-hour descent/five-hour return. Each mark represents one hour; playback is accelerated. The mule is an illustration.</p></details></div>\n</section>\n",
